# Cheatsheet

The kernel subset on one page. Each card links to its section of
[the kernel subset reference](../language.md), which has the exact rules.

## Kernels
{: .col-2}

### Define and call

```elixir
defmodule Geo do
  use Defk

  defk dot(a :: [f64], b :: [f64]) :: f64 do
    n = min(len(a), len(b))

    for i <- 0..(n - 1)//1, reduce: 0.0 do
      acc -> acc + a[i] * b[i]
    end
  end
end
```

```elixir
iex> a = <<1.0::float-64-native, 2.0::float-64-native>>
iex> Geo.dot(a, a)
5.0
```

[Defining a kernel](../language.md#2-defining-a-kernel)

### Options

| Write | Effect |
|---|---|
| `use Defk` | imports `defk` |
| `use Defk, elixir_mode: true` | adds `__defk_elixir__/2` outside `:test` |
| `use Defk, report: :full` | adds clang's vectorisation to the fast-path report |
| `defk f(...) :: t, yield: false do` | no safepoints: only for sub-millisecond kernels |

### Generated per module

| Function | Gives |
|---|---|
| `__defk_elixir__(:f, args)` | one call in Elixir mode |
| `__defk_c_source__/0` | the generated C |
| `__defk_report__/0` | the fast-path report as data |
| `__defk_stats__/0` | `frames_live`, `promotions`, `yields` |
| `__defk_force_yields__/1` | testing: yield at every safepoint |
| `__defk_lib__/0` | the native library's path |

[What `use Defk` generates](../language.md#what-use-defk-generates)

## Types
{: .col-2}

### Scalars and arrays

| Type | In Elixir |
|---|---|
| `i64` | integer in -2^63..2^63-1 |
| `u64` | integer in 0..2^64-1 |
| `f64` | float (an `i64` argument converts) |
| `bool` | `true` or `false` |
| `[f64]` `[f32]` `[i64]` `[i32]` `[i16]` `[u8]` `[u64]` | binary of packed native-endian elements |
| `{t1, t2}` | tuple, as a result only |
| `bitstring` | result of a bitstring accumulator |

Narrow element types read as `i64` or `f64`; a write that doesn't fit
raises. [Types](../language.md#3-types)

### Packing in Elixir

| Element | Build | Read |
|---|---|---|
| `f64` | `<<x::float-64-native>>` | `for <<x::float-64-native <- bin>>, do: x` |
| `i64` | `<<x::signed-64-native>>` | `for <<x::signed-64-native <- bin>>, do: x` |
| `u64` | `<<x::unsigned-64-native>>` | `for <<x::unsigned-64-native <- bin>>, do: x` |
| `u8` | `:erlang.list_to_binary(xs)` | `:binary.bin_to_list(bin)` |

Build a whole array with `for x <- xs, into: <<>>, do: <<x::float-64-native>>`.

## Expressions
{: .col-2}

### Operators

| Kind | Forms |
|---|---|
| arithmetic | `+ - * /` `div` `rem` (`/` gives `f64`) |
| comparison | `== != < > <= >=` |
| boolean | `and` `or` `not` |
| bitwise | `band bor bxor bnot bsl bsr`, or `&&& \|\|\| <<< >>>` |
| arrays | `a[i]`, `out[i] = v`, `len(a)` |

`i64` and `u64` overflow raises `ArithmeticError`; a float that would be inf
or NaN raises too. [Expressions](../language.md#4-expressions-and-operators)

### Builtins

- `len`, `min`, `max`, `abs`
- `float`, `trunc`, `round`
- `sqrt`, `exp`, `log`, `sin`, `cos`, `pow` (also `:math.sqrt/1` ...)
- `alloc(type, n)`: a new zero-filled array
- `wrap64`, `mulhi`, `clz`, `ctz`, `popcount`, `rotl`, `rotr`, `rotl64`, `rotr64`
- `u64_le(bytes, i)`, `u32_le`, `u16_le` and `_be`: word loads
- `bit_size(acc)`

[Builtins](../language.md#builtins)

### Wrapping arithmetic

```elixir
defk fnv1a(bytes :: [u8]) :: u64 do
  for b <- bytes, reduce: 0xCBF29CE484222325 do
    h -> band(bxor(h, b) * 0x100000001B3, 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF)
  end
end
```

```elixir
iex> M.fnv1a("a")
12638187200555641996
```

`+ - *` and bit operations inside `band(expr, 2^k - 1)` wrap and give
Elixir's exact masked result. [Masked arithmetic](../language.md#masked-arithmetic)

### Literals and constants

- A string or `<<1, 2, 3>>` is a read-only `[u8]`.
- `@name` holding a number or boolean is inlined; one holding a binary is a
  `[u8]`.

[Module attributes](../language.md#module-attributes)

## Control flow
{: .col-2}

### Branches

```elixir
defk sign(x :: i64) :: i64 do
  cond do
    x > 0 -> 1
    x < 0 -> -1
    true -> 0
  end
end
```

```elixir
iex> M.sign(-7)
-1
```

`if` needs an `else` when used as a value; `case` matches `i64` or `bool`
against literals, `^pinned`, `_` and variables, with guards.
[Control flow](../language.md#7-control-flow)

### Loops

| Form | Use |
|---|---|
| `for x <- a do ... end` | statement over an array |
| `for i <- 0..(n - 1)//1 do` | over a range (write the step) |
| `for x <- a, reduce: acc0 do acc -> ... end` | fold, also with a tuple accumulator |
| `Enum.reduce_while(a, acc, fn x, acc -> {:cont, acc} end)` | early exit |
| `Enum.all?(a, fn x -> ... end)`, `Enum.any?/2` | early exit |

### Early exit

```elixir
defk first_negative(a :: [i64]) :: i64 do
  Enum.reduce_while(0..(len(a) - 1)//1, -1, fn i, acc ->
    if a[i] < 0, do: {:halt, i}, else: {:cont, acc}
  end)
end
```

```elixir
iex> M.first_negative(<<4::signed-64-native, -2::signed-64-native>>)
1
```

### Output of unknown length

```elixir
defk evens(a :: [i64]) :: bitstring do
  for x <- a, reduce: <<>> do
    acc -> if rem(x, 2) == 0, do: <<acc::bitstring, x::64>>, else: acc
  end
end
```

```elixir
iex> M.evens(<<1::signed-64-native, 2::signed-64-native, 4::signed-64-native>>)
<<2::64, 4::64>>
```

Or `alloc` the largest size and return `{out, count}`.
[The bitstring accumulator](../language.md#the-bitstring-accumulator)

## Common rewrites
{: .col-1}

### Write this instead

| Written first | Write instead | Code |
|---|---|---|
| `Enum.sum(a)` | `for x <- a, reduce: 0.0 do acc -> acc + x end` | [`unsupported-call`](../language.md#unsupported-call) |
| `a \|> f(b)` | `f(a, b)` | [`pipe`](../language.md#pipe) |
| `for x <- a, do: x * 2` as a value | `out = alloc(f64, len(a))`, write `out[i]`, return `out` | [`for-collect`](../language.md#for-collect) |
| `[x \| acc]` then `Enum.reverse/1` | a bitstring accumulator, or `{out, count}` | [`unsupported-list`](../language.md#unsupported-list) |
| `for {x, i} <- Enum.with_index(a)` | `for i <- 0..(len(a) - 1)//1` and `x = a[i]` | [`generator-pattern`](../language.md#generator-pattern) |
| `<<a, b, rest::binary>> = bin` | `a = bin[0]`, `b = bin[1]` | [`bitstring-match`](../language.md#bitstring-match) |
| `x ** 2` | `x * x`, or `pow(x, 2)` | [`unsupported-expression`](../language.md#unsupported-expression) |
| `length(a)`, `byte_size(a)` | `len(a)` | [`unknown-function`](../language.md#unknown-function) |
| `unless c do` | `if not c do` | [`unsupported-construct`](../language.md#unsupported-construct) |
| a hash that wraps at 64 bits | `band(expr, 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF)` | [masked arithmetic](../language.md#masked-arithmetic) |
| maps, strings, atoms | pack values into binaries in Elixir first | [`unsupported-map`](../language.md#unsupported-map) |

The full table: [Unsupported, write this instead](../language.md#unsupported-write-this-instead).

## Testing
{: .col-2}

### Agreement

```elixir
Defk.Test.assert_agrees(Mod, :fun, args)
Defk.ElixirMode.with_mode(:elixir, fn -> Mod.fun(x) end)
Mod.__defk_force_yields__(true)
```

See [Testing kernels](testing.md).

### Explaining speed

```elixir
Defk.Report.print(Mod)
```

See [Measuring](measuring.md).
